WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.200 --> 00:00:05.552
We caught the spy, recovered the NVIDIA chip,
and thought this nightmare was over. But Mei Lin
just told us something terrifying.

00:00:06.200 --> 00:00:07.856
You caught the wrong enemy.

00:00:15.200 --> 00:00:23.048
And while we were fighting to save our operation, the real
NVIDIA scandal was shaking the tech world. Jensen Huang
had stepped down as CEO. Colette Kress was named interim CEO.

00:00:23.800 --> 00:00:26.008
Wait… this is happening in the real world too?

00:00:26.800 --> 00:00:29.128
Yes. But our mission is about to get even crazier.

00:00:29.330 --> 00:00:33.194
Guys! Someone just activated a remote computing network.

00:00:33.394 --> 00:00:34.762
How long before it goes live?

00:00:34.962 --> 00:00:41.538
We have only fifteen minutes before this unknown system
connects to thousands of AI processors. If we fail, we may
never find out who controls it.

00:00:41.740 --> 00:00:51.076
You recovered one chip. Congratulations. But you have no idea
how many systems are already connected.

00:00:51.280 --> 00:00:52.600
Who are you?

00:00:52.800 --> 00:00:58.032
That voice knows our security codes. This isn't an outside
attack. Someone has access from inside.

00:01:00.200 --> 00:01:04.472
I found three server locations connected
to the same administrator account.

00:01:05.200 --> 00:01:10.000
These aren't normal connections. They're routing
computing requests through different locations.

00:01:10.800 --> 00:01:15.432
We have three possible locations, but only one leads
to the mastermind. Team, split up!

00:01:16.200 --> 00:01:22.992
This is our first challenge. Ryan checks security, Mike
investigates the hardware, and Daniel traces the data.
We have three minutes to find the real server.

00:01:23.800 --> 00:01:24.928
I'm going underground.

00:01:25.800 --> 00:01:27.696
I'm checking the chip connections.

00:01:28.600 --> 00:01:29.968
And what am I supposed to do?

00:01:30.800 --> 00:01:32.168
Find out who gave them access!

00:01:33.000 --> 00:01:35.736
This room is empty! Someone sent us to the wrong location.

00:01:36.600 --> 00:01:39.984
Wait. If this is a decoy, someone knew exactly
where we would look.

00:01:40.800 --> 00:01:42.240
Predictable.

00:01:43.000 --> 00:01:47.200
These accounts are requesting huge amounts
of AI computing power.

00:01:48.000 --> 00:01:48.888
Who owns them?

00:01:49.800 --> 00:01:53.592
That's the problem. They all lead
to the same hidden account.

00:01:54.400 --> 00:01:59.368
The mastermind isn't just looking for a chip. They're trying
to control the computing power behind an entire AI network.

00:02:00.200 --> 00:02:03.272
Mei Lin, you said we caught the wrong enemy.
Tell us what you know.

00:02:04.200 --> 00:02:09.432
I was hired to take one chip. I was never told
what the network was for.

00:02:10.200 --> 00:02:11.472
Who hired you?

00:02:12.200 --> 00:02:16.616
I never saw their face. They called
themselves... The Architect.

00:02:17.400 --> 00:02:22.488
Guys! The Architect used our original
administrator credentials.

00:02:23.200 --> 00:02:25.072
That account was supposed to be deleted!

00:02:25.800 --> 00:02:29.616
Someone has been hiding in our system since the first
episode. And now we have to find out who.

00:02:30.600 --> 00:02:34.128
If we lock everything, we could lose
the tracking signal.

00:02:34.800 --> 00:02:38.400
Let me access the system. I can identify
the real server.

00:02:39.200 --> 00:02:41.120
Absolutely not! She's the spy!

00:02:42.000 --> 00:02:45.648
We have to choose. Trust our enemy or risk
losing the mastermind forever?

00:02:46.400 --> 00:02:49.232
I say we hear her out. She's the only one
who knows the operation.

00:02:50.000 --> 00:02:51.248
She's manipulating us!

00:02:52.000 --> 00:02:55.120
Her information matches the access logs.

00:02:55.800 --> 00:02:59.208
Fine. We'll give her sixty seconds. But if she lies,
the mission is over.

00:03:00.200 --> 00:03:08.624
The Architect never needed to steal every chip. The plan was
to access computing power from different locations and hide
who was using it.

00:03:09.400 --> 00:03:11.704
A hidden AI network!

00:03:12.400 --> 00:03:17.680
Now it makes sense. The real challenge isn't finding one stolen
chip. It's finding who controls the entire network.

00:03:18.400 --> 00:03:21.136
No! It's wiping the access history!

00:03:21.800 --> 00:03:24.392
The Architect knows we're tracking them.

00:03:25.200 --> 00:03:27.576
You should have stayed out of this.

00:03:28.400 --> 00:03:32.240
Mike, stop the deletion! Ryan, secure the room!
We are not losing this evidence!

00:03:33.000 --> 00:03:36.168
Thirty seconds! We have one chance to isolate the network
before the final connection.

00:03:36.900 --> 00:03:38.124
I'm at the main power room!

00:03:38.800 --> 00:03:40.672
I need the access key!

00:03:41.400 --> 00:03:45.888
I found it! But the key belongs
to our original founder account!

00:03:46.600 --> 00:03:51.832
Guys... this account was created before
the entire investigation started.

00:03:52.600 --> 00:03:54.496
So this person planned everything?

00:03:54.800 --> 00:03:59.888
They knew about the security vault, the stolen chip, and even
our recovery mission. This was never a random attack.

00:04:00.200 --> 00:04:01.856
Connection isolated!

00:04:02.600 --> 00:04:04.160
All remote access is blocked!

00:04:04.900 --> 00:04:08.332
YES! We stopped the transfer! But wait...
where is The Architect?

00:04:15.200 --> 00:04:21.344
You are looking for a person. But you should have
been looking at the system.

00:04:22.000 --> 00:04:23.176
That's impossible...

00:04:23.900 --> 00:04:28.628
The administrator account was controlled
by the experimental AI system!

00:04:29.400 --> 00:04:32.832
The system itself was helping someone hide the network.
But who built it?

00:04:33.600 --> 00:04:38.424
You stopped one network. You haven't stopped
the people who created me.

00:04:39.200 --> 00:04:40.856
People? There are more of them?

00:04:41.600 --> 00:04:44.912
I told you. I was never the mastermind.

00:04:45.600 --> 00:04:47.040
Then who is controlling this thing?

00:04:47.800 --> 00:04:56.416
We caught the spy. We stopped the network. But now we've
discovered something much bigger. Someone built an AI system
that can hide its own creators. And it just started Phase Two!

00:04:57.200 --> 00:04:59.576
Thank you for finding me.

